In article <13344.28132970@ecs.umass.edu> bryant@ecs.umass.edu writes:
]	What do statues do???  There was some guy in a room with a bunch of
] centaur statues.  I gave him 50 g.p. and he told me some number.  What does
] this do and does it have anything to do with the statues you find lying

Well, usually statues look pretty, remind you of famous people,
and are moderately heavy things to carry around.
Usually they're just made of stone, but sometimes they're hollow
with things inside.  How would you find out?

What uses can you find for a large heavy stone object?

And sometimes they look like people you know!
Why would a statue of YOUR system administrator be hanging around
deep in the dungeon?  And who is that Maud person, anyway?

As for the woman with the fountain and bunch of statues,
you've met the Oracle at Delphi!  (You could probably have found
this out with the / command; use ? for help.)
She can tell your fortune for a small fee, though they say that
	"Not all fortunes are as deceitful as this one".

You can talk to people (and animals, and walls, ..) with #chat. 
What does the Oracle say if you talk to her?  Can you trust her? 
Can she be bribed into telling you more?   Is killing her a good idea?
Does she taste good?  What happens if you talk to other people?

Anyway, if you're into statues, Delphi is the place to go.

